108
00:03:59,378 --> 00:04:01,206
Here a student asks about residues.

109
00:04:05,436 --> 00:04:07,441
A residue is essentially the coefficient

110
00:04:07,441 --> 00:04:09,446
of the one over z term in the Laurent

111
00:04:09,446 --> 00:04:11,611
series expansion of your function around a

112
00:04:11,611 --> 00:04:12,220
singularity.

113
00:04:12,974 --> 00:04:14,658
The residue theorem makes life easy

114
00:04:14,658 --> 00:04:16,102
because it allows you to replace a

115
00:04:16,102 --> 00:04:18,042
difficult path integral with a simple sum

116
00:04:18,042 --> 00:04:21,169
of these residues multiplied by two pi i.

117
00:04:21,169 --> 00:04:23,238
It turns complex calculus into a much

118
00:04:23,238 --> 00:04:25,452
simpler problem of algebraic evaluation.

119
00:04:26,264 --> 00:04:29,077
To recap: AssemblyAI text to speech

120
00:04:29,077 --> 00:04:31,070
